# No git checkout / git restore

**Never run `git checkout` or `git restore`.** Any arguments, any paths, including
`HEAD`, `--`, `--staged`, `--worktree`, `--ours`, `--theirs`, single files,
generated lang, or “just to isolate a commit”. There is no exception for
cleaning a diff, undoing an edit, runData pollution, or mixed WIP.

Do not use `git reset --hard`, `git reset -- <paths>`, `git clean`, or
`git stash` of uncommitted work either. This agent does not get to decide
that a destructive git command is safe.

Switch branches with `git switch` / `git switch -c` only when the user asked
to change branch. Do not switch in order to discard files.

# Commit mixed WIP together

If the user asks to commit and the tree has more than one piece of work,
`git add` the dirty tracked files and new work, then one commit. Do not
split cards or leave “other” dirty files out.

Still skip secrets, `run/`, `.idea/`, and gitignored evidence dumps.
